     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-05 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>2027 ODI World Cup Qualifiers Set for South Africa and Namibia</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#WorldCupQualifiers</span> <span>#ODI</span> <span>#Cricket</span></div>
       <p>South Africa and Namibia will co‑host the 2027 ODI World Cup Qualifiers, a ten‑team tournament scheduled from 26 February to 21 March 2027. The event will decide which nations join the automatically qualified sides for the 2027 ODI World Cup.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/2027-odi-world-cup-qualifiers-set-for-south-africa-and-namib.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The dates were confirmed at ICC meetings in Dubai in late September 2026 after the schedule was trimmed from an earlier window of 22 February‑23 March. The revised window fits neatly between two major domestic leagues: the SA20 tournament ends on 21 February, and the IPL 2027 season runs from 14 March to 30 May, with its main phase expected to start at the end of March.</p><p>South Africa and Zimbabwe have already secured automatic World Cup spots as co‑hosts of the main event. They are joined by eight pre‑qualified full‑member teams – India, New Zealand, Pakistan, Australia, England, Sri Lanka, Afghanistan and Bangladesh. The qualifier field also includes West Indies, Ireland (qualified via September 2026 ODI rankings), and the top four from the World Cricket League Division 2: Scotland, USA, Netherlands and Oman.</p><p>A separate playoff slated for 1‑22 December will determine additional participants, featuring the bottom four Division 2 sides (Namibia, Canada, Nepal, UAE) and the four highest‑placed Challenge League teams (Italy, Uganda, Jersey, Kuwait). Namibia, as a co‑host, can earn a direct World Cup berth by beating USA and UAE twice each from 3 October, provided results among Oman, Nepal and Canada fall in its favour. The qualifier winner advances straight to the World Cup group stage, while the next three contest a Super Series in Namibia for a second spot.</p><p>What to watch: the outcome of the qualifier and the Super Series that will decide the final two World Cup entrants.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The report is accurate and efficiently covers all key details from the source, including the qualification pathway and the specific dates.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/2027-world-cup-qualifiers-to-be-held-in-south-africa-and-namibia-from-february-26-7050/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
