     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-10-05 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Alia Bhatt and Carlos Sainz Reunite for L’Oréal Elvive Haircare Campaign</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Entertainment</span> <span>#Bollywood</span> <span>#Advertising</span></div>
       <p>Bollywood actress Alia Bhatt and Formula 1 driver Carlos Sainz have reunited for a L’Oréal advertisement, months after their much-discussed meeting at the Cannes Film Festival earlier this year. Their latest collaboration, promoting L’Oréal’s new Elvive haircare range, has surfaced on social media and is currently being widely circulated by fans, prompting an enthusiastic response online.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/alia-bhatt-and-carlos-sainz-reunite-for-loreal-elvive-hairca.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The initial encounter between Bhatt and Sainz at Cannes had already generated considerable online interest, with fans speculating about a potential professional partnership. That possibility has now materialized with their joint appearance in this new campaign. While the advertisement does not appear to have had an official release in India, the video has quickly gained traction across social media platforms. An Italian promo featuring the duo for L’Oreal Paris was shared on X by @leclercsainz_1655 on September 30, 2026.</p><p>Professionally, Alia Bhatt continues to have a busy schedule with multiple projects. She recently starred in &quot;Alpha,&quot; marking her entry into the YRF Spy Universe, and also expressed satisfaction over the release of &quot;Don’t Be Shy,&quot; which premiered on Amazon Prime Video. Her upcoming films include Sanjay Leela Bhansali’s &quot;Love &amp; War,&quot; a period drama co-starring her husband Ranbir Kapoor and Vicky Kaushal, slated for release in January next year. Bhatt has also completed work on &quot;Tumbbad 2,&quot; where she is set to appear in a new avatar.</p><p>This brand collaboration with Carlos Sainz adds another dimension to Alia Bhatt’s ongoing professional engagements, which encompass both film commitments and various endorsements. Her latest appearance alongside the Formula 1 driver provides a fresh talking point for her extensive fan base across social media.</p><p>What to watch: Official release details and further collaborations from the duo.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft covers the L'Oreal ad collaboration and provides relevant, fact-checked background on Bhatt's professional projects.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/features/alia-bhatt-reunites-with-f1-star-carlos-sainz-for-loreal-ad-after-cannes-meeting-video-goes-viral/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
