     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-10-05 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge conf" title="Reported by Bollywood Hungama, TOI Entertainment">confirmed by 2 sources</span></div>
       <h1>Ayushmann Khurrana starrer Udta Teer postponed to October 23</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Udta Teer</span> <span>#Ayushmann Khurrana</span> <span>#Bollywood</span> <span>#Film Release</span></div>
       <p>The theatrical release of the film Udta Teer, starring Ayushmann Khurrana, has been rescheduled from its original date of October 9 to October 23. According to veteran trade analyst Taran Adarsh on X, the makers opted for this two-week delay to secure a clearer release window. Bollywood Hungama reports that the decision aims to avoid a crowded marketplace and provide the film with more open theatrical space. The shift allows the production team to conduct further promotional activities leading up to the new October 23 weekend slot.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/ayushmann-khurrana-starrer-udta-teer-postponed-to-october-23.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Directed by Akash A Kaushik in his directorial debut, the film features a unique storyline where Ayushmann Khurrana portrays a Pakistani spy who loses his identity and ends up supporting India, according to TOI Entertainment. This distinct character follows the actor's trend of playing diverse roles. The supporting cast includes Sara Ali Khan, Gulshan Grover, Mukul Dev, and Ram Kapoor. The makers believe the additional time will help present the film to audiences during a period with fewer competing major releases.</p><p>Filmmakers and studios involved with Udta Teer continue to assess the theatrical calendar to maximize the movie's commercial potential. By moving away from the October 9 date, the team expects to capitalize on a less congested window for the project. The title and initial promotional materials have already generated significant interest, and the team is now focused on building momentum toward the revised late-October launch. Both trade sources and the film's team agree that the change provides a better theatrical opportunity.</p><p>What to watch: Promotional materials and trailers expected to release before October 23.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately synthesizes the provided source and supplementary context, maintaining a professional tone and covering all essential details.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>How this was reported · 2 sources</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/ayushmann-khurrana-starrer-udta-teer-postponed-to-october-23/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ayushmann-khurrana-and-sara-ali-khans-udta-teer-postponed-amid-gondhal-previews-giving-it-a-cleaner-release-window/articleshow/134641701.cms" rel="noopener">TOI Entertainment</a></li></ul>
      <p>Synthesised from 2 independent reports on the same event. Details are attributed to the outlet that carried them; nothing outside these sources is published.</p>
    </div>
       
