     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · TOI Entertainment · 2026-10-05 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge conf" title="Reported by TOI Entertainment, Bollywood Hungama">confirmed by 2 sources</span></div>
       <h1>Blockbuster 'Hanuman Ansh' Set for Worldwide Telugu Release on October 9</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Entertainment</span> <span>#Film Release</span> <span>#Box Office</span> <span>#Telugu Cinema</span></div>
       <p>The small-budget film ‘Hanuman Ansh,’ which unexpectedly grossed over Rs 400 crore worldwide, is now slated for its global Telugu release on October 9, 2026. Following its strong reception among Hindi-speaking audiences, the spiritual drama will now reach Telugu audiences, with the announcement made by the makers of blockbusters like the ‘Kantara’ and ‘KGF’ franchises, and ‘Salaar’.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/blockbuster-hanuman-ansh-set-for-worldwide-telugu-release-on.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Hombale Films, which is releasing ‘Hanuman Ansh’ in Telugu, alongside Swambhu Media Network as presenters, posted on Instagram, expressing delight to bring the “much loved #HanumanAnsh in TELUGU, for audiences to witness its divine brilliance on the big screen across the world.” The film has garnered attention for its portrayal of faith and spiritual awakening, according to Bollywood Hungama. Written and directed by Vishal Chaturvedi, the movie delves into the life and spiritual legacy of Neem Karoli Baba, featuring Shobhinav Satyaa and Chandan Anand in lead roles, with Nikhil Dubey, Udaysinh Rajput, and Purnima Tiwari in supporting capacities.</p><p>Despite its modest budget, 'Hanuman Ansh' experienced a slow start at the box office before gaining significant momentum. According to trade tracker Sacnilk, the film collected Rs 2.90 crore net in India on Day 56 across 4,345 shows. Its total India gross collection reached Rs 374.86 crore, with a net collection of Rs 317.38 crore. Overseas, the film added Rs 10 lakh on Day 56, bringing its total overseas gross to Rs 39.20 crore, contributing to its impressive worldwide gross of Rs 414.06 crore.</p><p>This success positions ‘Hanuman Ansh’ as a notable achievement in Indian cinema. The production house behind it is also involved in several major upcoming projects, including Prabhas’ ‘Salaar: Part 2 – Shouryaanga Parvam,’ ‘Suriya 48,’ and an anticipated collaboration with Bollywood star Hrithik Roshan.</p><p>What to watch: The film's box office performance in the Telugu market.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Strong entertainment report utilizing box office data, release dates, and production details accurately from the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>How this was reported · 2 sources</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/telugu/movies/news/makers-of-kantara-kgf-salaar-to-bring-telugu-release-of-hanuman-ansh-worldwide-release-on-october-9/articleshow/134638084.cms" rel="noopener">TOI Entertainment</a></li><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/south-cinema/hombale-films-to-release-hanuman-ansh-in-telugu-on-october-9/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>Synthesised from 2 independent reports on the same event. Details are attributed to the outlet that carried them; nothing outside these sources is published.</p>
    </div>
       
