     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-05 · editor 6/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>CEC Gyanesh Kumar Faces Protests in Delhi and Mumbai; Pilot Hailed for Foiling Flydubai Hijack</h1>
       
       <p>Protests have erupted against Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar in Mumbai and Delhi, with the Citizens Justice Party (CJP) demanding his resignation. In Mumbai, the CJP, led by founder Abhijeet Dipke, organized a gathering at Shivaji Park in Dadar. Protesters pressed three principal demands: Kumar's resignation, the freezing of the 2025 electoral list, and complete transparency in appointing future election chiefs. Large crowds, including youths and first-time voters from various parts of Maharashtra, gathered with national tricolours and placards despite lacking formal police permission. Security forces maintained a heavy presence at the site. The CJP plans further agitations across six other cities, culminating in an indefinite demonstration at Jantar Mantar in New Delhi by late October. Earlier demonstrations in the national capital saw Delhi Police detaining over 1,100 political and student activists.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/cec-gyanesh-kumar-faces-protests-in-delhi-and-mumbai-pilot-h.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Meanwhile, calls have mounted to confer India's highest peacetime gallantry award, the Ashok Chakra, on Captain Smit Machchhar, the FlyDubai pilot hailed for foiling a hijack attempt. Captain Machchhar saved more than 170 passengers on a flight between Dubai and Tel Aviv. Shiv Sena leader and Member of Parliament Milind Deora has written to Prime Minister Narendra Modi on behalf of Eknath Shinde and his party, urging consideration for the Mumbai-based civilian aviator. Deora noted that Captain Machchhar's actions brought pride to Mumbai and India, drawing parallels with Neerja Bhanot, who received the Ashok Chakra after the 1986 Pan Am hijack. He emphasized that celebrating such bravery inspires future generations. The decision on civilian and military gallantry awards remains subject to evaluation by the central government and the Ministry of Defence.</p><p>Podcaster Zalak Mehta spoke about her viral podcast interview with Captain Machchhar, highlighting his reflections on the importance of flight crew and onboard doctors during medical emergencies, noting his consistent prioritization of passenger safety. Mehta recalled his grounded nature and dedication, stating, &quot;What really stayed with me was his humility.&quot; Pilot Tina Goswami, a former colleague, analyzed Captain Machchhar's extraordinary presence of mind and courage during the mid-air cockpit attack. Goswami explained the operational severity, noting that Captain Smit managed to set the emergency transponder squawk code, stating, &quot;Thereafter, he put 7500, which is unlawful interference.&quot; She highlighted his actions despite negative G-forces and fighting off an attacking co-pilot in a confined space, prioritizing opening the cockpit door to save everyone on board.</p><p>A potential Iranian involvement in the Flydubai flight hijack bid is being investigated, raising concerns over severe escalation across West Asia involving Israel, the United States, and Sunni Gulf nations. The discussion notes that the pilot involved is Omani, highlighting regional flight agreements and Muscat's delicate diplomatic position. Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu cited &quot;radicalisation and jihadist ideology&quot; behind the attempt. Observers suggest that while Israel remained the target near the anniversary of the October 7 attacks, the plot also posed a major risk to the Abraham Accords and ties between Israel and the United Arab Emirates.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft combines two unrelated stories into one article, which is confusing and poor journalistic practice. It covers most facts but fails to separate the distinct topics.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/video/protests-against-cec-gyanesh-kumar-in-delhi-and-mumbai-cjp-demands-resignation-ytvd-3008240-2026-10-02?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
