       <h1>Charlie Harmison signs two-year professional deal with Durham</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Charlie Harmison, the 18-year-old son of 2005 Ashes winner Steve Harmison, has signed a two-year rookie contract with Durham. The fast bowler joins other sons of former Ashes winners in signing professional terms with County Championship clubs, including Archie Vaughan and the Flintoff brothers.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/charlie-harmison-signs-two-year-professional-deal-with-durha.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Following Durham’s promotion to the top flight after winning the Division Two title, Harmison expressed excitement for the upcoming challenge. The club also confirmed rookie deals for 19-year-old wicketkeeper-batter Robbie Bowman and 18-year-old batter Luke Symington.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise, accurate, and includes all relevant details from the source text.</p>
