     <article class="story single" data-beat="business">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · Economic Times · 2026-10-05 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick Discloses $250 Million in Income</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#business</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>US Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick reported at least $250 million in income for 2025, his first year in government. A major portion of this total included a $192 million tax distribution from Cantor Fitzgerald, the firm he led for decades before joining the Trump administration.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/commerce-secretary-howard-lutnick-discloses-250-million-in-i.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Additional earnings included $19.6 million from a Newmark partnership unit exchange and $14.1 million in salary and bonuses from BGC Group. Lutnick, who divested from leadership roles at numerous organizations upon his confirmation in February 2025, also reported selling at least $259 million in assets and purchasing $166 million in securities, maintaining his status as one of the wealthiest Cabinet members.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the financial disclosure, though it omits the specific detail that the $192 million was a tax distribution. It remains well within the target length.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/international/global-trends/us-news-at-27-howard-lutnick-helped-make-300-million-decades-later-he-reports-250-million-in-income-as-trumps-commerce-chief/articleshow/134639817.cms" rel="noopener">Economic Times</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
