       <h1>Congo's Ebola Death Toll Exceeds 4,000 Amidst Containment Struggles</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Ebola</span> <span>#Congo</span> <span>#Outbreak</span> <span>#Public Health</span></div>
       <p>Congo's ongoing Ebola outbreak has now surpassed 4,000 recorded deaths, according to authorities. This grim milestone comes as officials continue to struggle with containing the spread of the deadly virus across the region.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/congos-ebola-death-toll-exceeds-4000-amidst-containment-stru.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The challenges in managing the outbreak have been compounded by significant incidents on the ground. An Ebola treatment center was recently burned down, further hindering efforts to control the disease and provide care to those affected.</p><p>Authorities are intensifying their efforts amidst the rising death toll and operational difficulties. The situation highlights the complex public health crisis facing Congo.</p><p>What to watch: Updates on containment efforts and security around treatment facilities.</p>
       
