     <article class="story single" data-beat="defence">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-10-05 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Defence Secretary Rajesh Kumar Singh Reveals $600 Million in BrahMos System Buyers</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence Exports</span> <span>#BrahMos System</span> <span>#Rajesh Kumar Singh</span> <span>#India</span></div>
       <p>India's Defence Secretary, Rajesh Kumar Singh, has announced that the country has secured buyers for its advanced BrahMos missile system, totaling a significant sum of $600 million. This revelation highlights India's growing footprint in the global defence export market.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/defence-secretary-rajesh-kumar-singh-reveals-600-million-in-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The BrahMos system, a supersonic cruise missile, is a key product in India's defence manufacturing capabilities. The identification of $600 million worth of buyers underscores international interest in India's indigenous defence technology and its strategic importance.</p><p>This development marks a notable achievement for India's defence sector, signaling successful efforts in promoting and exporting its military hardware.</p><p>What to watch: Further details on the specific buyers and future defence export agreements.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Solid, concise report correctly utilizing the source details regarding Defence Secretary Rajesh Kumar Singh and the $600M BrahMos buyers.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
