     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-05 · editor 7/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Education Ministry Launches Rs 5.4 Crore Challenge for Innovative Ideas</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#Innovation</span> <span>#Government Scheme</span> <span>#Funding</span></div>
       <p>The Education Ministry has announced a new challenge, offering a substantial fund of Rs 5.4 crore for innovative ideas. This initiative aims to encourage creativity and problem-solving within the education sector.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/education-ministry-launches-rs-54-crore-challenge-for-innova.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The challenge, as reported by India Today, invites individuals and groups to submit their innovative concepts. The allocated Rs 5.4 crore is intended to support and develop groundbreaking ideas that could benefit educational practices and outcomes.</p><p>What to watch: Details on application criteria and submission deadlines for the challenge.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate to the source provided, though very brief due to the limited nature of the source material.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5&amp;hl=en-US&amp;gl=US&amp;ceid=US:en" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
