     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-10-05 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Flydubai Captain Praised for Defusing Passenger Retaliation During Mid-Air Crisis</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Dr. Maya Peretz, a passenger on the September 30 Flydubai flight where a captain was stabbed by his co-pilot, has praised Captain Smit Machchhar for his calm leadership. While injured, Machchhar instructed passengers to stop attacking the subdued co-pilot, urging them to focus on stabilizing the aircraft instead. The plane safely diverted to Tabuk, Saudi Arabia.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/flydubai-captain-praised-for-defusing-passenger-retaliation-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Following emergency surgery, Machchhar was airlifted to Abu Dhabi, where he is recovering and in stable condition. Dr. Peretz commended his immense humanity and presence of mind, noting she hopes her daughter will grow up to possess his values.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the crisis, the captain's leadership, and his recovery status using provided facts.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/leave-co-pilot-focus-on-plane-flier-dr-maya-peretz-recounts-injured-captain-smit-machchhars-words-wants-daughter-to-be-like-him-ws-klrt-10364669.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
