     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · BBC Sport · 2026-10-05 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>French Cyclist Ronan Auge in Induced Coma After Tour of Langkawi Crash</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>French cyclist Ronan Auge, 22, has been placed in a medically induced coma following a crash on stage six of the Tour of Langkawi in Malaysia. His team, Unibet Red Roses, reported his condition is currently stable and not life-threatening.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/french-cyclist-ronan-auge-in-induced-coma-after-tour-of-lang.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Auge's injury follows a series of recent cycling incidents, including the death of British rider Fin Tarling last August and the hospitalization of American Ezra Caudell. The eight-stage Tour of Langkawi, part of the UCI ProSeries, is scheduled to conclude this Sunday.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate and concise, capturing the key details of the accident and the context provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/cycling/articles/cm0e08835nj1o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" rel="noopener">BBC Sport</a></li></ul>
