     <article class="story single" data-beat="science">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SCIENCE</span> · Phys.org · 2026-10-05 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Genetic Research Reveals Causes of Aurochs Extinction</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#science</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>New research from Lund University indicates that the aurochs, ancestors of modern cattle, faced multiple stressors leading to their extinction. A population bottleneck during migration to Scandinavia reduced their genetic diversity, while the flooding of a land bridge 8,000 years ago isolated the population. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/genetic-research-reveals-causes-of-aurochs-extinction.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Combined with intense human hunting, these factors caused a sharp decline in the Swedish population. The species eventually disappeared from Sweden around 6,500 years ago as their open-landscape habitats transitioned into dense forests. This decline culminated in their final global extinction in 17th-century Poland.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately synthesizes the research findings and timeline provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://phys.org/news/2026-10-aurochs-genetic-evidence-reveals-multiple.html" rel="noopener">Phys.org</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-10-05/genetic-research-reveals-causes-of-aurochs-extinction" data-title="Genetic Research Reveals Causes of Aurochs Extinction"><b>Share:</b>
