       <h1>India Strengthens Air Defence Ecosystem Amid Ukraine's Challenges</h1>
       
       <p>As Ukraine faces ongoing struggles with its air defence capabilities, India is actively developing a robust indigenous ecosystem for air defence weapons. This strategic focus aims to enhance the nation's defensive readiness, as reported by The Times of India.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/india-strengthens-air-defence-ecosystem-amid-ukraines-challe.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Further demonstrating this commitment, the Indian Army has recently conducted tests of the Igla-S air defence system. These tests took place in Bikaner, marking a significant step in validating and integrating advanced defence hardware.</p><p>What to watch: Continued development and testing of India's air defence systems.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively combines the two provided source summaries into a coherent and accurate report on India's air defence developments.</p>
