     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-10-05 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India to Face Defending Champions China in Asian Games 2026 Women's Hockey Final</h1>
       
       <p>India is poised to compete against defending champions China in the gold medal match of women's hockey at the Asian Games 2026. This significant final is scheduled for Friday, October 2 (IST), and will commence at 3:30 PM IST. The Gifu Prefectural Green Stadium in Kakamigahara, specifically the Gifu Prefectural Hockey Stadium, will host the high-stakes encounter. The match carries importance beyond the medal itself, as the victorious team will also secure an automatic berth at the Los Angeles 2028 Olympic Games. Both India and China have reached this summit clash as unbeaten teams, having navigated distinct challenges throughout the tournament.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/india-to-face-defending-champions-china-in-asian-games-2026-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>India's historical performance in women's hockey at the Asian Games includes only one gold medal, won in 1982. Since that achievement, the team has advanced to the final on two subsequent occasions, in 1998 and 2018, where they ultimately secured silver medals after being defeated by South Korea and Japan, respectively. The upcoming match offers India an opportunity to add a second gold to its record and achieve direct Olympic qualification. The game will be televised live on the Sony Sports Network, and live streaming will be accessible via the SonyLIV app and website.</p><p>In other sporting developments, a historic international football friendly is set to take place on Saturday, featuring India against Brazil at the Salt Lake Stadium in Kolkata. The IFA Shield Semi-Final will also see Mohun Bagan compete against Punjab FC (MBSG vs PFC). Looking ahead, the Asian Games 2026 will conclude with its closing ceremony on Sunday. Shooting star Neeru Dhanda, who has earned two gold medals and one silver, has been named India's flag bearer for the closing event, marking the formal end of the Games.</p><p>What to watch: India's pursuit of Olympic qualification and a second Asian Games women's hockey gold.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately synthesizes the provided information about the hockey final and integrates the additional news items provided in the source summary.</p>
