       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-10-05 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>India's BrahMos Exports Projected to Exceed $600 Million</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#BrahMos</span> <span>#Exports</span></div>
       <p>India's Defence Secretary has announced that the nation's exports of the BrahMos missile system are projected to surpass $600 million, Livemint reports. This statement highlights a significant milestone in India's growing defence manufacturing and export capabilities.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/indias-brahmos-exports-projected-to-exceed-600-million.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The BrahMos missile, a key defence asset, is attracting international buyers, contributing to the substantial export figures. While specific purchasing nations were not detailed in the summary, the Defence Secretary's remarks underline the increasing global demand for Indian defence technology.</p><p>What to watch: Future expansion of defence exports.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Succinctly reports the projection provided in the source.</p>
