       <h1>Mahindra and Embraer Plan C-390 Assembly Line in India for IAF Order</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#Aerospace</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Mahindra</span></div>
       <p>Mahindra and Embraer are reportedly planning to establish an assembly line for the C-390 aircraft in India. This strategic move is specifically aimed at securing a potential order from the Indian Air Force (IAF), as reported by The Times of India.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/mahindra-and-embraer-plan-c-390-assembly-line-in-india-for-i.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The collaboration signifies a push towards indigenous manufacturing within the defence sector, aligning with broader national objectives. The C-390 is a specific aircraft model being targeted for this production facility within India.</p><p>Their joint venture anticipates meeting the IAF's requirements by localizing the assembly process, potentially enhancing India's defence industrial base and reducing reliance on foreign imports for military hardware.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reflects the source summary provided.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
