     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-05 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Mississauga, Toronto, Vancouver Secure Wins on Canada Super 60 Day 3</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#Canada Super 60</span> <span>#T20 Cricket</span> <span>#Sports</span></div>
       <p>Mississauga Masters, Toronto Sixers, and Vancouver Anchors all recorded victories on Day 3 of Canada Super 60 Season 2 at BC Place on October 2, 2026. The day was highlighted by star performances from Sikandar Raza, Nicholas Pooran, and Moeen Ali across the men's fixtures. Vancouver Warriors Women also secured a win in the day's women's match.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/mississauga-toronto-vancouver-secure-wins-on-canada-super-60.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Vancouver Anchors initiated the men's victories, bowling out Brampton Blitz for 84/9 in 10 overs. They then chased the target, reaching 90/4 in 8.4 overs, winning by six wickets. Moeen Ali led the reply with an unbeaten 37 off 18 balls, including one four and four sixes at a strike rate of 205.56, supported by Obus Pienaar's 22 off 13 balls. Lewis Gregory was instrumental with the ball, taking 4/13 from two overs, while Martin Andersson and Akhil Kumar each claimed two wickets.</p><p>Toronto Sixers followed suit, successfully chasing White Rock Warriors' 128/6 with three balls to spare, finishing on 129/5 in 9.3 overs to win by five wickets. White Rock's innings featured Aryan Sidhu's 40 off 16 balls and Dominic Drakes' unbeaten 38 off just 10 deliveries. Nicholas Pooran anchored Toronto's chase with an explosive 40 off 16 balls at a strike rate of 250, hitting five sixes. Kieron Pollard added 22 off nine balls, and Daniel Sams contributed an unbeaten 27 off 10 balls, also taking 2/26 with the ball.</p><p>Mississauga Masters secured the closest win of the day, posting 125/2 before restricting Montreal Royal Tigers to 123/4, winning by two runs. Sikandar Raza was the standout performer for the Masters, reaching his half-century off just 24 balls. This victory left Mississauga Masters unbeaten after their opening two men's matches in the league phase. On Day 4, Zaheer Khan co-owned Vancouver Anchors and Sikandar Raza-led Mississauga Masters both secured semi-final berths, according to Crictracker. Mississauga Masters later finished the league stage unbeaten on 10 points on Day 5, also according to Crictracker.</p><p>In the women's fixture, Vancouver Warriors Women defeated Vancouver Anchors Women by eight wickets. Anchors Women posted 81/4 in 10 overs, with Fatima Sana Khan top-scoring with 49 off 31 balls. Sophie Reid led the Warriors' chase with an unbeaten 37 off 16 balls, alongside Marizanne Kapp's 14 not out off seven, reaching 82/2 in 7.4 overs. Toronto Sixers Women later clinched their second successive title on Day 5, beating Vancouver Warriors Women by six wickets, as per Crictracker.</p><p>What to watch: The upcoming semi-final matches and the conclusion of Canada Super 60 Season 2.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Comprehensive summary of the match results and statistics, effectively integrating additional context from the supplementary reports.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
