     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-05 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Rest of India Gains Significant Lead on Day 3 Against Jammu &amp; Kashmir in Irani Cup 2026</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#Irani Cup</span> <span>#Match Review</span></div>
       <p>The Irani Cup 2026 has seen a significant shift in momentum, with Rest of India now leading Jammu and Kashmir by 265 runs at the close of Day 3, according to Crictracker. This follows an impressive bowling performance on Day 2, Friday, October 2, which initially saw Rest of India trailing by 17 runs against Jammu and Kashmir.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/rest-of-india-gains-significant-lead-on-day-3-against-jammu-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>On Day 2, Jammu and Kashmir's captain Paras Dogra delivered a crucial batting display at the Sher-i-Kashmir Stadium in Srinagar, scoring a well-composed 75 off 143 balls, including six fours and one six. Dogra formed a vital 101-run partnership with Abdul Samad, who contributed a valuable 57 runs. Towards the end of the innings, Lone Nasir Muzaffar continued to build momentum with an impressive 64, helping J&amp;K establish their position.</p><p>The bowling efforts for Rest of India were spearheaded by left-arm pacer Mukesh Choudhary, who made the most of the conditions on Day 1, securing a superb five-wicket haul with figures of 5/78. Choudhary dismissed key batsmen including Qamran Iqbal, Shubham Pundir, Shubham Khajuria, Paras Dogra, and Kanhaiya Wadhawan. He received strong support from Akash Deep, who claimed three wickets for 43 runs, and Mukesh Kumar, who chipped in with two wickets for 84 runs, collectively restricting Jammu and Kashmir's batting progress.</p><p>While Day 2 concluded with Rest of India trailing by 17 runs, the subsequent play on Day 3 has seen a dramatic turnaround, pushing Rest of India into a commanding lead of 265 runs by stumps. This reversal underscores the dynamic nature of the Irani Cup match and sets up an intriguing final phase.</p><p>What to watch: How Jammu &amp; Kashmir responds to the significant deficit on Day 4.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively integrates the source text with the additional context provided about the Day 3 results.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/irani-cup-2026-jammu-kashmir-vs-rest-of-india-highlights-review-day-2-9992/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/jammu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Jammu</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
