     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · TechCrunch · 2026-10-05 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Rivian Recalls R2 SUV Over Battery Fastener Defect</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Rivian has issued a recall for its R2 SUV due to improperly tightened high-voltage battery pack fasteners that could cause power loss. Approximately 14 vehicles are affected, and the company has already reprogrammed its Normal, Illinois assembly line to prevent future defects. Rivian stated it is unaware of any injuries or accidents related to the issue.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/rivian-recalls-r2-suv-over-battery-fastener-defect.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This is the second recall for the R2, which began shipping this year to facilitate the company's push for mass-market profitability. Rivian aims to deliver 20,000 to 25,000 units by year-end, marking one of the fastest U.S. EV launches despite early manufacturing challenges.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate and concise, correctly identifying the recall scope and context provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/02/rivian-issues-r2-recall-for-poorly-tightened-battery-packs/" rel="noopener">TechCrunch</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
