       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-05 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Search Operation Underway for Three Boys at Rushikonda Beach</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A search operation is underway at Rushikonda beach in Visakhapatnam after three 14-year-old boys were swept away by strong waves on Friday. The students, part of a group from Madhurawada, were playing in the sea when they were pulled into deeper water.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/search-operation-underway-for-three-boys-at-rushikonda-beach.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Marine police, local swimmers, and a specialized scuba-diving team have been deployed to the site near the IT SEZ junction to locate the missing students. Police Commissioner Shankhabrata Bagchi is personally monitoring the rescue efforts, with further details regarding the identities of the boys currently pending.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the search operation details and the status of the missing boys as reported by the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Visakhapatnam/three-boys-swept-away-at-visakhapatnams-rushikonda-beach-search-on/article71536893.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
