       <h1>WB NEET UG 2026 Counselling: Round 3 Choice Filling Begins, Allotment October 8</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#NEET UG</span> <span>#Counselling</span> <span>#West Bengal</span></div>
       <p>The West Bengal National Eligibility cum Entrance Test Undergraduate (WB NEET UG) 2026 counselling process has commenced its Round 3 choice filling phase. This marks a crucial step for candidates seeking admission, as reported by The Times of India.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-05/wb-neet-ug-2026-counselling-round-3-choice-filling-begins-al.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Following the choice filling period, the seat allotment for this round is scheduled to take place on October 8. These developments are for the 2026 academic year admissions.</p><p>This stage of counselling is vital for students to secure their preferred medical and dental college seats in West Bengal, progressing towards the final allocation.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft concisely covers all provided facts from the summary.</p>
